A||N||4||loafer87gt||Running on 3 Cylinders!!!||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||04-14-2000||12:36 PM||||I have been without my FieroGT for over two weeks now!! For some reason, when you run the car abd drive around, then shut it off and let it sit for 15 minutes, when you fire it up again it is only running on three cylinders. So far the GM dealership has replaced the ECM, the MAP sensor, EGR sensor, plugs, plugwires, distributor, ignition module, coil, cap and rotor, and it is still doing it. I also had the injectors cleaned about a month back, and the alternator replaced last fall. They said they have checked every bit of wiring in the car but still can't seem to track down the problem. Does anyone have any ideas, I am really getting frustrated with my my Fiero and the GM dealership.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||04-14-2000||01:38 PM||||The injectors are powered using two separate circuits, one for each bank of 3 cylinders.  It is obvious from this that your problem is  a short, bad connection, or fuse (there is one fuse for each circuit bank) in one of these two circuits.  The heat dependence of the malfunction is interesting, and may indicate a short in close proximity to the engine.  If the fault is reproducible, it is simply a matter of tracing each circuit for continuity to locate the problem area.<P>Mike B.<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 04-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiasco||04-14-2000||09:01 PM||||First things first...<BR>In my experience, dealerships hate Fieros.<BR>If they ever do find that short like Mike was talking about, they'll prob. try to stick ya for a whole new wiring harness!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||daved||04-15-2000||12:36 AM||||Easy thing to do...change both injector fuses in case one is opening up intermittently.<BR>When the problem occurs, disconnect the flat plug by the thermostat housing.  Check the wiring loom end, A to B & C to D with a test lamp, to make sure ECM is energising each bank of injectors (lamp flashes rapidly).<BR>Let us know the result. D.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero_86_se||04-16-2000||01:43 AM||||I had one that did that too,   the problem was a warped head.....you think that may be a possibility?||||reg||1
